# ==========================================================
# VIVA QUESTIONS WITH ANSWERS
# ==========================================================

# 1. What is Git?
# Git is a distributed version control system used to track code changes.

# 2. What is GitHub?
# GitHub is a cloud platform used to store and manage Git repositories online.

# 3. What is version control?
# Version control tracks changes in files and allows rollback to previous versions.

# 4. Difference between Git and GitHub?
# Git = tool
# GitHub = online hosting platform for Git repositories

# 5. What is repository?
# Repository is a storage location containing project files and Git history.

# 6. What does git init do?
# Initializes a new local Git repository.

# 7. What does git add do?
# Adds files to staging area before commit.

# 8. What does git commit do?
# Saves snapshot of project changes.

# 9. What does git push do?
# Uploads local repository code to GitHub.

# 10. What is staging area?
# Temporary area where files are prepared before commit.

# 11. What is branch?
# Separate development line in Git.

# 12. What is clone?
# Copying remote repository to local system.

# 13. What is pull?
# Downloads latest changes from GitHub.

# 14. What is commit message?
# Short description explaining code changes.

# 15. Why GitHub is used?
# For collaboration, backup, version tracking and project hosting.


# ==========================================================
# THEORY
# ==========================================================

# Git:
# Open-source version control software.

# GitHub:
# Online hosting service for Git repositories.

# Workflow:
# Working Directory -> Staging Area -> Commit -> GitHub Repository

# Advantages:
# 1. Tracks code history
# 2. Easy collaboration
# 3. Backup of code
# 4. Multiple developers can work together
# 5. Easy rollback


